      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The numerator's degree is not less than the denominator's, so divide first: \\( \\frac{3 x^{2}}{x^{2} + 3 x + 2} = 3 + \\frac{- 9 x - 6}{x^{2} + 3 x + 2} \\), and write \\( \\frac{- 9 x - 6}{x^{2} + 3 x + 2} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2} \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Clearing denominators gives \\( - 9 x - 6 = A \\left(x + 2\\right) + B \\left(x + 1\\right) \\). Setting \\( x = -1 \\) gives \\( A = 3 \\), and setting \\( x = -2 \\) gives \\( B = -12 \\), so the integrand is \\( 3 - \\frac{12}{x + 2} + \\frac{3}{x + 1} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
